{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "e48657af-5c83-41ee-9474-05b36ba61caa",
    "name": "Quipu Tenant Service",
    "description": "Complete REST API collection for the Quipu Tenant Service microservice (port 3031, context path /admin). This is the multi-tenant management / provisioning control-plane: owns tenant lifecycle (create -> config -> activate/deactivate) and orchestrates Keycloak, Vault, per-tenant PostgreSQL, and audit ingestion.\n\nCollection variables:\n- {{baseUrl}}  — default http://localhost:3031/admin (note the /admin context path)\n- {{token}}    — bearer JWT sent as Authorization header; also decoded server-side by JwtTokenFilter to populate the User-Id request attribute used by POST /tenant\n- {{tenantId}} — tenant identifier (X-Tenant-ID header, used by /tenant/user-status)\n\nTypical flow:\n1. POST /tenant                      → create tenant (provisions Keycloak realm/client/user, emits TENANT_CREATED)\n2. PUT  /tenant/config/{tenantId}    → configure tenant (Vault populate + Postgres DB creation)\n3. PUT  /tenant/{tenantId}/{active}  → activate/deactivate tenant\n4. GET  /tenant, /tenant/active, /tenant/{code} → lookups\n\nNotes:\n- All /tenant endpoints (except /tenant/users/{tenantCode} and /tenant/user-status) produce application/vnd.quipu.tenant+json;version=1.0.0.\n- /audit endpoints produce application/vnd.quipu.audit+json;version=1.0.0.\n- No bean validation — validation is manual server-side; there is no pagination on any list endpoint.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "56383100",
    "_collection_link": "https://go.postman.co/collection/56383100-e48657af-5c83-41ee-9474-05b36ba61caa?source=collection_link"
  },
